  "en": {
   "stanzas": [
    [
     "I know you by the edge",
     "of the sword, the fearsome one,",
     "I know you by the look",
     "that measures the earth with force."
    ],
    [
     "Brought forth from the bones,",
     "the sacred ones, of the Greeks,",
     "and valiant as at first,",
     "hail, O hail, Liberty!"
    ],
    [
     "In there you dwelt,",
     "embittered, shamefaced,",
     "and you waited for a mouth",
     "to say to you, «come again»."
    ],
    [
     "That day was slow to come,",
     "and all was silent,",
     "because threat cowed them",
     "and slavery weighed them down."
    ],
    [
     "Unhappy one! The only consolation",
     "left to you was to tell of",
     "past glories",
     "and, telling of them, to weep."
    ],
    [
     "And waited and waited",
     "for a liberty-loving voice,",
     "one hand struck the other",
     "out of despair,"
    ],
    [
     "And you said: «When, ah, when shall I lift",
     "my head out of the desolate places?»",
     "And there answered from above",
     "laments, chains, cries."
    ],
    [
     "Then you raised your gaze,",
     "clouded in tears,",
     "and on your garment blood dripped,",
     "a multitude of Greek blood."
    ],
    [
     "With your clothes bloodied",
     "I know that you went out in secret",
     "to seek in foreign lands",
     "other, strong hands."
    ],
    [
     "Alone you took the road,",
     "alone you came back again;",
     "doors are not easy",
     "if need knocks on them."
    ],
    [
     "One wept on your breast,",
     "but no relief at all;",
     "another promised you help",
     "and deceived you horribly."
    ],
    [
     "Others, alas, at your misfortune",
     "who rejoiced greatly,",
     "«go and find your children,",
     "go», said the cruel ones."
    ],
    [
     "The foot flees backward",
     "and very swiftly treads",
     "either the stone or the grass",
     "that reminds you of your glory."
    ],
    [
     "Most humbly droops",
     "your thrice-wretched head,",
     "like a pauper's who knocks from door to door",
     "and whose life is a burden to him."
    ],
    [
     "Yes, but now there fights back",
     "every child of yours with vigour,",
     "who ceaselessly seeks",
     "either victory or death."
    ],
    [
     "Brought forth from the bones,",
     "the sacred ones, of the Greeks,",
     "and valiant as at first,",
     "hail, O hail, Liberty!"
    ],
    [
     "As soon as it saw your onrush,",
     "the sky, which for the enemies",
     "in your mother earth",
     "nourished flowers and fruits,"
    ],
    [
     "grew calm; and there poured forth",
     "a roar from beneath the earth,",
     "and of Rigas there answered you",
     "the war-shouting voice."
    ],
    [
     "All your lands called out to you,",
     "greeting you warmly,",
     "and the mouths cried out",
     "all that the heart felt."
    ],
    [
     "They cried out to the stars,",
     "the islands of the Ionian too,",
     "and raised their hands",
     "to show joy,"
    ],
    [
     "although it is chained,",
     "each one, cunningly,",
     "and on its forehead written",
     "it has: «False Liberty»."
    ],
    [
     "Heartily rejoiced",
     "the land of Washington too,",
     "and remembered the irons",
     "that bound it also."
    ],
    [
     "From its tower it cries out,",
     "as if to say, I greet you,",
     "and shakes its mane,",
     "the Spanish lion."
    ],
    [
     "Startled like a deer was England's",
     "beast, and at once it sends",
     "towards the ends of Russia",
     "the roars of its wrath."
    ]
   ],
